      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14249141/assets/a60731e7df54bb8f18f834b818c3e49c79fb30e67f7ed50c40f40aa813689ece.png)\n\nA manufacturer produces an unfair tetrahedral die from a plastic net, shown above. What is the total surface area of the die?",
      "worked_solution": "The net shown corresponds to a triangular pyramid. The surface area of our pyramid consists of $1$ base triangle and $3$ side triangles. \n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Surface area} & =1\\times (\\text{Area of base})+3\\times (\\text{Area of side}) \\\\  & =1\\times 64+3\\times 78 \\\\  & =64+234 \\\\  & =298\\,{\\text{mm}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
